# The backend this frontend is built and tested against.
#
#   repo   owner/name on GitHub, or a path to a local clone
#   ref    a commit, a branch or a tag
#
# Both sides changing at once: push the backend branch, point ref at it, push the
# frontend branch - CI builds that commit and tests against it. On merge, move ref
# to the merged commit.
#
#   repo = LukasZahradnik/NeuraLogic      somebody else's fork, no extra permission needed
#   ref  = my-feature-branch              a branch, while the work is in flight
#   repo = ../NeuraLogic                  a local clone, for a branch pushed nowhere yet
#
# A commit can be checked against the jar's stamp offline, and a branch cannot -
# scripts/backend_jar.py --check says which of the two it did. So a branch is for work
# in flight; what lands should name a commit.
#
# The script also takes --jar PATH to install a jar you already built, which needs
# neither network nor Maven.

repo = GustikS/NeuraLogic
ref = 18eaa7e00423c141ec4412f62a017bda240f9e20
